# Remand's "if that spell is countered this way" is conditional, "draw a card" is not: Abrupt Decay can't be countered (CR 101.2), so
# it resolves and destroys Bot1's Mox Sapphire, is not returned to hand (it goes to Bot2's graveyard), and Bot1 still draws.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Remand
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Emerald
Abrupt Decay
Swamp x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Abrupt Decay.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Remand.Cast(Abrupt Decay)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Abrupt Decay
Bot1.Graveyard = Mox Sapphire; Remand
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
